From aebf3eb64b9c525e77a99405f8a97aa254b335e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: santanumahata <santanuedu.m@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:28:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NanoAOD: let photon TrigObj keep objects from the unseeded
 e/gamma collection

The Photon selection of triggerObjectTable only accepted trigger objects
whose collection is hltEgammaCandidates. The unseeded-leg filters of
HLT_Diphoton30_22_R9Id_OR_IsoCaloId_AND_HE_R9Id_Mass90 (and Mass95),
    hltEG22R9Id85b90eHE12R9Id50b80eR9UnseededLastFilter
    hltEG22Iso60CaloId15b35eHE12R9Id50b80eTrackIsoUnseededLastFilter
(and hltEG18TrackIso60...TrackIsoUnseededFilter), run on
hltEgammaCandidatesUnseeded, so their objects were rejected by the
selection before the quality bits were evaluated. The corresponding
TrigObj_filterBits were therefore defined but could never be set for
photons (bits 14/15 in NanoAODv13, 16/17 here), which breaks trigger
matching of the subleading diphoton leg.

Accept both collections, as the Electron selection already does since
PR #41827. With skipObjectsNotPassingQualityBits=True only unseeded
objects that pass one of the photon filters are added, and the
producer's self-cleaning merges them with the seeded duplicate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QJYkW4qPckDhLoe6VfCP28
---
 PhysicsTools/NanoAOD/python/triggerObjects_cff.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/PhysicsTools/NanoAOD/python/triggerObjects_cff.py b/PhysicsTools/NanoAOD/python/triggerObjects_cff.py
index 2691ff0e8..6239ec1de 100644
--- a/PhysicsTools/NanoAOD/python/triggerObjects_cff.py
+++ b/PhysicsTools/NanoAOD/python/triggerObjects_cff.py
@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@ triggerObjectTable = triggerObjectTableProducer.clone(
         ),
         Photon = cms.PSet(
             id = cms.int32(22),
-            sel = cms.string("type(92) && pt > 15 && coll('hltEgammaCandidates')"),
+            sel = cms.string("type(92) && pt > 15 && (coll('hltEgammaCandidates') || coll('hltEgammaCandidatesUnseeded'))"),
             l1seed = cms.string("type(-98)"),  l1deltaR = cms.double(0.3),
             #l2seed = cms.string("type(92) && coll('')"),  l2deltaR = cms.double(0.5),
             skipObjectsNotPassingQualityBits = cms.bool(True),
